# Continuous health on the Meridian slice (#71), 30 September 2026.
# kind, stock Sveltos v1.15.0, ConfigHub. `cub sveltos` built from this
# repository after v0.9.0.
#
# Sveltos runs a delivery profile's validateHealths only when it deploys. A
# HealthCheck and a ClusterHealthCheck keep watching: part A measured that
# with a hand-written check, and part B with the one `cub sveltos apply` now
# writes, read by `cub sveltos status`.
#
# Part A was run by hand at 07:02 to 07:08 and is transcribed here from its
# output. Part B is the recording as captured. During part B the laptop ran
# sixteen kind clusters at a load average of 18 on 18 cores, and Kyverno's
# pods on the Meridian clusters were restarting on their own ("unable to
# apply cgroup configuration"). The check found that too, which is why test1
# had not recovered by the end of part B.

== A. A probe: one HealthCheck for Kyverno's Deployments, on the six clusters (07:02:16)
-- The first attempt returned each resource's health under healthStatus, as
-- the HealthCheck field's description says. Sveltos's agent refused every
-- report: 'spec.resourceStatuses[0].healthStatus: Unsupported value: ""'.
-- The agent reads the key status; with it, all six clusters passed:
eu-central-prod1: kyverno-workloads=True, addons=True
eu-central-prod2: kyverno-workloads=True, addons=True
eu-central-prod3: kyverno-workloads=True, addons=True
eu-central-prod4: kyverno-workloads=True, addons=True
eu-central-test1: kyverno-workloads=True, addons=True
eu-central-uat1: kyverno-workloads=True, addons=True
-- 07:06:06 test1's node cordoned, and the cleanup controller's pod deleted, so its replacement stays Pending
-- 07:06:43, 37s later, on eu-central-test1:
kyverno-workloads=False: Deployment: kyverno/kyverno-cleanup-controller status is Degraded Message: kyverno-cleanup-controller: 0 of 1 available
addons=True
-- the ClusterSummary: kyverno-eu-central-test1-sveltos-eu-central-test1 Provisioned
-- the Addons liveness check stays True: it follows what Sveltos deployed, not whether it is running
-- 07:06:55 the node uncordoned
-- 07:07:41, 46s later: kyverno-workloads=True, addons=True
-- Kubernetes events from the ClusterHealthCheck: Warning on eu-central-test1 when it failed, Normal when it recovered

