Management cluster mgmt/mgmt
  record   mer-management  one delivery profile per variant (6): each sends its variant's releases to its one cluster
  health   a ClusterHealthCheck per profile (1): watches the workloads it delivers on its clusters, after each release too

In ConfigHub
  7 Targets in mer-targets, one per cluster, on a server-hosted worker
  1 component, each one base, 3 class bases, 6 variants, 1 management record
  12 Spaces and 9 Links, one tying each unit of a class base or a variant to its upstream (check your organization's quotas for both first)
  first rollout: kyverno in 3 stages after its class bases; one approval per stage, one release per variant

Note: kyverno-test's chart kyverno has 11 Helm hooks for upgrade, delete or test, among them Jobs kyverno-migrate-resources, kyverno-rm-webhooks, kyverno-scale-to-zero. They are left out, as cub helm leaves them out, because only Helm runs them.

Wrote onboard-ch/apply.sh and the files it reads. Read it, then run it:
  MGMT_CONTEXT=<kubectl context of your management cluster> bash onboard-ch/apply.sh
$ grep -E '^  (record|health) ' onboard-ch/plan.txt
  record   mer-management  one delivery profile per variant (6): each sends its variant's releases to its one cluster
  health   a ClusterHealthCheck per profile (1): watches the workloads it delivers on its clusters, after each release too
